@node The package
@section The package

Clone the repository anywhere and put it on Emacs's load path:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "~/path/to/narrate")
(require 'narrate)
(keymap-global-set "C-c n" 'narrate-command-map)   ; any free prefix
(with-eval-after-load 'dired
  (keymap-set dired-mode-map "C-c N" #'narrate-dired))
@end lisp

Or with @samp{use-package} and @samp{:vc} (Emacs 30):

@lisp
(use-package narrate
  :vc (:url "https://github.com/offgridauthor/narrate")
  :bind-keymap ("C-c n" . narrate-command-map))
@end lisp

@samp{make info} builds the Info manual from this file; with the repository on @samp{Info-additional-directory-list}, @samp{C-h i} lists narrate like any other package (package managers that install from the repository do this on their own).

The Emacs side runs the backend with @samp{narrate-python}, which defaults to a venv at @samp{~/.local/share/narrate/venv} when there is one and @samp{python3} otherwise. A venv keeps engine packages (and their large dependencies) out of the system Python:

@example
python3 -m venv ~/.local/share/narrate/venv
~/.local/share/narrate/venv/bin/pip install pymupdf
@end example

From a shell, @samp{narrate-cli} in the repository runs the backend without installing anything, and @samp{pip install .} (or @samp{pip install -e .}) installs it as a @samp{narrate} command.

@node Profiles
@section Profiles

Copy @samp{profiles.example.toml} to @samp{~/.config/narrate/profiles.toml} and edit it. It starts on the @samp{dry-run} profile, which ticks instead of speaking, so the whole path from book to M4B can be checked before any engine is installed. @samp{NARRATE_CONFIG}, or @samp{narrate-profiles-file} in Emacs, points at a profiles file somewhere else; the folder it sits in is narrate's config folder.

@node API keys
@section API keys

Cloud engines read their keys from the environment. In Emacs, @samp{narrate-auth-hosts} also fills them from auth-source, e.g. in @samp{~/.authinfo.gpg}:

@example
machine generativelanguage.googleapis.com login apikey password YOUR-GEMINI-KEY
machine api.speechify.ai login apikey password YOUR-SPEECHIFY-KEY
@end example

A variable already set in the environment wins.

@node Engines
@chapter Engines

Each engine is optional; profiles whose engine can't run report themselves unavailable, and their fallbacks take over.

