@node Files and folders
@section Files and folders

narrate follows the XDG base directory layout:

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem folder
@tab holds
@item @samp{~/.config/narrate/}
@tab @samp{profiles.toml}, @samp{voices.json}, @samp{breeze-voices/}, @samp{tryout-designs.txt}, @samp{plugins/}
@item @samp{~/.local/share/narrate/}
@tab the Python venv, Breeze-TTS-2.cpp and its models
@item @samp{~/.cache/narrate/}
@tab auditions, previews, tryouts, the Breeze server log, the live GPU-share setting
@end multitable

@samp{XDG_CONFIG_HOME}, @samp{XDG_DATA_HOME}, and @samp{XDG_CACHE_HOME} move them, and @samp{NARRATE_CONFIG} puts the profiles file (and so the config folder) anywhere, such as a synced folder. A render's chunk cache lives in @samp{.narrate-work/} inside the output folder.

@node Extending
@chapter Extending

Python files in @samp{plugins/} beside the profiles file load at startup. A plugin can add engines and input readers; @samp{examples/plugins/} has one of each.

An engine subclasses @samp{narrate.engines.base.Engine}, sets @samp{name}, and implements:

@itemize
@item
@samp{prepare()} checks it can run here and raises @samp{EngineUnavailable} if not
@item
@samp{identity()} returns a string naming the voice exactly; it keys the chunk cache
@item
@samp{synth(text)} returns 24 kHz mono 16-bit WAV bytes, raising @samp{Refused} for text it can't voice, @samp{Transient} for retryable failures, and @samp{RateLimited} when asked to slow down
@end itemize

Class attributes tell narrate the rest: @samp{max_chars} (chunk size), @samp{check_length} (re-roll audio far too short or long for its text), @samp{uses_gpu} (@samp{gpu_share} applies), and @samp{remote} (where text goes when it leaves the machine, shown before sending). @samp{narrate.engines.register(cls)} makes it available as @samp{engine = "NAME"}.

A reader is a function from a @samp{Path} to a @samp{narrate.book.Book}; @samp{narrate.readers.register(".ext", func)} ties it to an extension. @samp{narrate.book.build_chapters} turns a list of @samp{(heading level or None, text)} pairs into chapters the way the built-in readers do.

The backend's pieces are small modules (@samp{readers/}, @samp{engines/}, @samp{chunking}, @samp{synth}, @samp{assemble}, @samp{commands}, @samp{cli}), so a different front end, or a different kind of output, can reuse them.

@node Privacy
@chapter Privacy

@itemize
@item
Engines that run here (@samp{tone}, @samp{breeze}, @samp{kokoro}) send nothing anywhere.
@item
Engines that don't (@samp{gemini}, @samp{speechify}) send each chunk's text to their service. narrate asks before a cloud profile renders a book or auditions selected text (@samp{narrate-confirm-cloud}); stock passages go without asking.
@item
Fallbacks can cross that line: a profile on this machine whose fallback is a cloud profile will send text if the local engine can't run. Keep private work on profiles whose whole fallback chain stays local.
@item
Keys live in the environment or auth-source, never in the profiles file.
@end itemize

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@table @asis
@item A profile says it's unavailable
@samp{narrate-show-log} has the reason (no key, a package missing, no model, a server that didn't start). @samp{narrate-cli profiles} lists each profile's engine and fallbacks.
@item Breeze won't start
@samp{~/.cache/narrate/breeze-server.log} has the server's own output.
@item Chapters look wrong
@samp{RET} in the outline shows the extracted text. DOCX chapters come from heading styles, so titles typed as bold body text won't register; @samp{E} exports the text to Org for fixing by hand. A part only splits into chapters when its chapters have headings one level below the part's.
@item No cover in the finished book
a cover image ffmpeg can't embed is skipped, with a line in the log saying so; the audio and chapters are unaffected.
@item The mode line shows no time left
the estimate appears after a minute or so of progress, once there's a pace to measure.
@item Formats narrate doesn't read
convert first, e.g. @samp{soffice --headless --convert-to docx file.odt} (also .doc and .rtf) or Calibre's @samp{ebook-convert book.azw3 book.epub} (also .mobi).
@end table

